# Terminology glossary: pipe-delimited, columns en|ru|ru_pattern|note.
# "#"-prefixed and blank lines are comments, stripped before parsing.
#
# - en: EN term (word-boundary, case-insensitive match). Rows sharing an en
#   (e.g. duplicate senses, or an abbreviation alongside its spelled-out
#   form) are merged: any one row's translation counts as correct.
# - ru: canonical display translation, for humans -- not used for matching.
# - ru_pattern: what the checker matches, as space-separated tokens: a
#   `word<>` stems (matches any suffix, e.g. "таблиц<>" -> "таблица"/
#   "таблицы"/...); a bare `word` must match exactly (do-not-translate
#   terms, SQL keywords, abbreviations). All tokens must be present.
# - note: optional context for why the row exists. Informational only.
#
# AI/human readers using this as translation guidance (not via
# docs_tool.py): use columns en/ru/note only, ignore ru_pattern. Coverage
# is curated from observed drift, not exhaustive.
